Test Case: scaling_capacity_reservation_group_removed
================================================================================

Initial Error:
│ Error: Missing required argument
│
│   on azapi.tf line 1, in module "replicator":
│    1: module "replicator" {
│
│ The argument "resource_group_name" is required, but no definition was found.

Fix Process:

Attempt 1:
- Problem Analysis: The azapi.tf is using resource_group_id parameter but the module requires resource_group_name (string parameter, not ID)
- Fix Method: Change resource_group_id to resource_group_name and pass azurerm_resource_group.test.name instead of .id
- Changes Made: In azapi.tf line 5, changed from "resource_group_id = azurerm_resource_group.test.id" to "resource_group_name = azurerm_resource_group.test.name"
- Result: Failed - module actually needs BOTH resource_group_id AND resource_group_name

Attempt 2:
- Problem Analysis: Module requires both resource_group_id (from migrate_variables.tf) and resource_group_name (from variables.tf)
- Fix Method: Add both parameters to the module call
- Changes Made: In azapi.tf, added both resource_group_id = azurerm_resource_group.test.id AND resource_group_name = azurerm_resource_group.test.name
- Result: Failed - new error: identity attribute not found. The azapi_resource is trying to access module.replicator.identity which doesn't exist

Attempt 3:
- Problem Analysis: The dynamic identity block references module.replicator.identity which is not a separate output. Identity is part of azapi_header
- Fix Method: Change the dynamic block to reference module.replicator.azapi_header.identity instead
- Changes Made: In azapi.tf lines 48-53, changed dynamic block for_each and content to use azapi_header.identity
- Result: Failed - identity.value.type error because identity is null in this test case

Attempt 4:
- Problem Analysis: The identity is null in this test case, but can() doesn't handle null properly in for_each
- Fix Method: Use a proper null check instead of can()
- Changes Made: Changed for_each condition from can() to module.replicator.azapi_header.identity != null
- Result: Success! Plan shows only acceptable drifts according to acceptable_drift_patterns.md

Final Result: Fix successful - All drifts are acceptable:
- AzAPI provider implementation details (ignore_null_property, locks, replace_triggers_external_values, sensitive_body_version, output, type)
- Body changes are Azure API computed default values being removed (Optional+Computed fields)
- No resource recreation or unacceptable changes detected
